ants and  community safety environmental services  covers environmental health public  conveniences Street cleansing recycling  collection and communications in this  section you are given the cost of the  service and asked what level of  reduction you would make and your  choices are don't reduce reduce  marginally reduced significantly or  don't know there's also room to give  your comments section 2 asks whether  there are any services that you  currently receive where you'd be willing  to pay a fee in order to avoid further  reductions in service section 3 asks  whether you would be prepared to pay  more council tax if this would avoid  further reduction in services and  section 4 asks about you your sex  ethnicity age etc but you don't have to  answer the  if you prefer not to if you would find  it difficult to use a printed copy of  this survey then please do call Rochford  Council on 0170 2546 366 and they will  be happy to find a way to help you to  have your say all in a day's recycling  lorraine allison from stanbridge hates  to waste anything and reuses recycles  and composts everything she can that is  why she has been nominated as a local  recycling champion with three home  composter business lorraine can compost  her food scraps and garden waste to make  her own compost any additional garden  and food waste goes into her curbside  compostables thin which is green with a  yellow lead and is collected weekly all  food waste can be placed into this bin  including meat fish and bones as they  should not be placed into your own home  compost bin anything that isn't reused  is recycled and Anna rain makes sure she  washes all her bottles cans and food  containers before placing them loose  into her recyclables been electrical  items should not be placed into any of  the three curbside bins broken small  electrical items can be recycled at the  dedicated recycling bank in back lane  car park ruptured at any of the lmb  textile banks throughout the district  